Scope (owner decision 2026-10-15): the performance remainder only. Four of the card's seven goals landed
early (#107/#109/#123, `ShapeRange`). Streaming save is dropped unless the lazy-blob measurement shows that
save, not load, holds the memory. Cross-run text stays v0.7.0.

Source policy (owner decision 2026-10-15): lazy blobs for PATH sources only (zip reopened per read,
CRC/size checked, no lingering handle); stream and directory sources stay eager. Implementation
detail and the two confirmed audit leads (L1 stale shape-name index, L2 stale `sha1`) are in the card.

## Goals
- Lazy binary blobs: image and media parts (and other binary parts) keep a reference into the
  package zip and read their bytes only when `.blob` is first accessed. Today every part's bytes are
  read when the deck loads.
- Caching audit: review all 203 `@lazyproperty` uses (44 files; "204 in 45" also counted the decorator's docstring) for soundness, meaning no stale
  value after a mutation the API allows. Add a cache only where a hot path recomputes a derived
  collection, and only with a measured win (#51 showed `paragraphs`/`runs` caching is a loss).

